                    />
                    <byline
                            inlineVariations="uk-text-small"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                            text="Marcus Adair. Field reporter, has packed the same bag for ten years. 8 min read."
                    />
                </container>
            </hero>
            <body
                    inlineVariations="uk-section uk-section-default"
                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                    sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/section"
            >
                <container
                        inlineVariations="uk-container"
                        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                        sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/structure/container"
                >
                    <p0
                            inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                            text="Two weeks in a carry-on is not a stunt. It is a system. The system is: clothes you will actually wear, in colors that go with each other, in fabrics that wash in a hotel sink and dry overnight. Anything else is a hobby."
                    />
                    <p1
                            inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                            text="The list, every trip: four shirts, two pants, one pair of shorts, four pairs of socks, four pairs of underwear, one fleece, one rain shell, one swimsuit, one pair of shoes you walk in, one pair of sandals. Plus toiletries. Plus a small zip pouch for chargers. That is it."
                    />
                    <p2
                            inlineVariations="uk-text-lead"
                            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                            sling:resourceType="/libs/kestros/commons/components/content/text"
                            text="You will look at the list and think you are forgetting things. You are not. You are forgetting the things you would have bought anyway and never used. The bag you can actually carry is the trip you can actually take."
                    />
                </container>
            </body>
